  "details": "It seems like, (in current l-test) once the user changes the language to Simplified Chinese, the preset messages (MM > Notification > Edit message) would be locked in Simplified Chinese forever. It was unable to test this problem further due to the hard locking nature, and it was also unsure if this problem would show up for other language(s). \n\n**Please** share any information regarding this problem.\n\n**Edit:** (29 Jan.) \n\nMassive thanks to `nekochanfood` for sharing more information!\n\nThe preset messages seems to be locked to the set language when launching the client for the first time (after an `l-test`).\n\nI am curious if the preset messages would be overwritten by sequncial updates.\n\n**Edit:** (31 Jan.)\n\nAgain informed by `nekochanfood`. Looks like the issue is currently isolated to `l-test` versions. Changing to `open-beta` (1400) does fix the issue, but it comes back after switching back to `l-test` (1393).",
